    {
      "name": "medusa.create_listing",
      "description": "Create the marketplace LISTING from a product (create_product / import_products): one listing per variant SKU for one store and marketplace, origin erp; for a product with more than one variant the ERP also creates or reuses a non-buyable parent draft (family.parent_sku, family.parent_listing_id) and stores the variation theme — listings holds only the children. Report family, and family.reason when the family step did not run. Each listing takes its desired copy from the product and its profile unless overridden, stores its attributes and links its variant. Follow the installed Intgral listing skill (intgral-listing). Idempotent per (store, marketplace, SKU). Supply the confirmed store_id from /admin/amazon/stores; omission uses the backend default store, never the browser's selection. ES/Spanish defaults are backend pilot defaults; explicitly supply the confirmed marketplace/locale. Do not infer brand or market from the host or URL. Brand, manufacturer and condition need their own sources. Inspect the returned compliance report and batch missing or conflicting facts once before requested updates with update_listing. Never publishes; the ERP refuses to publish until ready.",
